  "id": "COMPOUND:18392 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "Topsentisterol D3 appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, MIP, which is the target of multiple compounds—Sophoradiol, Cycloeudesmol, and Poricoic Acid B. These compounds all lead to the activation of prostate cells, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the modulation of signaling pathways within prostate cells. The evidence indicates that Topsentisterol D3 may act through a common intermediate, MIP, to influence prostate cell function. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting MIP and ultimately prostate cells implies that the interaction may be mediated by a broader network of pathways, possibly involving the regulation of cellular processes such as proliferation or differentiation. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Topsentisterol D3 to exert its effects through a shared molecular mechanism, possibly involving the modulation of MIP-dependent signaling.",
